changes.after:
The retained network uses the raw 2ZC9 heavy- and light-chain alpha carbons, all 27 heavy atoms of ligand 22U, and Gly216 N, C and O in addition to its existing alpha carbon; hirugen chain I is optionally included. Every nearby pair has an equal central-force spring at the chosen 10-, 12- or 15-angstrom cutoff, including ligand-internal and ligand--protein pairs. The baseline spring scales are 1 and 2 in the prescribed model, without chemical fitting. Six rigid motions are projected out. This is an elastic-network model, not a chemically parameterised bonded Hessian: uniform ligand springs, dense intraligand connections and the absence of waters are model assumptions.

The X bundle joins ligand N1 to Gly216 N, alpha carbon, C and O. The alternative R bundles join D-Phe ring atoms C16--C21 to the alpha carbons of Leu99, Ile174 and Trp215 (the S3/S4 proxy), or chlorobenzyl atoms C10--C15/CL1 to those of Asp189, Ala190 and Gly219 (the S1 sensitivity alternative); only edges within the selected cutoff enter. The recorded X rank is 4 and R rank is 18 or 21 respectively. These ranks count independent gradient columns while preserving their weights, not just two rank-one perturbations. Neither pocket proxy establishes a Q substituent replacement.\footnote{Retained branch-3 network definition, entry 80; rank and model-assumption accounting, entries 82--83. The ranks and conventions are recorded model results, not a new calculation.}

The twelve restoration cases cross two hirugen choices, three cutoffs and two R proxies on the same inherited 2ZC9 geometry. They are parameter sensitivities, not independent structures or molecular validation replicates. Common proportional spring scaling is covered algebraically. The earlier 48 stiffening rows additionally varied spring and update scaling; they must not be counted as 48 independent validations or confused with these twelve restoring quartets.\footnote{Retained branch-3 counting corrections 92--93 and joint restoration entries 5, 7 and 9.}

The initial 22U model strengthened existing contacts.
